.sb-svg { display: block; margin: 2mm auto; }
.sb-ifthen { display: flex; flex-direction: column; margin-bottom: 2mm; }
.sb-ifthen-row { display: flex; align-items: flex-end; gap: 2mm; min-height: var(--sb-pitch); }
.sb-ifthen-w { flex: 0 0 auto; font: italic 400 11pt var(--sb-serif); padding-bottom: 0.6mm; }
.sb-ifthen-blank { flex: 1 1 0; min-width: 0; border-bottom: 0.4pt solid var(--sb-rule); padding: 0 1mm 0.6mm; font-size: 10pt; }

.sb-c-step { margin: 3mm 0 1mm; font: 400 10.5pt var(--sb-serif); } .sb-c-step b { font: 700 9pt var(--sb-mono); margin-right: 2mm; }
.sb-c-why { margin: 1mm 0; font: 600 9pt var(--sb-sans); }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<section class="sb-page" id="W1-P1" data-component="self-explain"><i class="sb-reg sb-tl"></i><i class="sb-reg sb-tr"></i><i class="sb-reg sb-bl"></i><i class="sb-reg sb-br"></i><header class="sb-ph"><span class="sb-pid">W1-P1</span><span class="sb-ptitle">Self-explain</span><span class="sb-ptag">self-explain</span></header><p class="sb-prompt">For each step, write why it follows. Don&#39;t restate it; justify it.</p><div class="sb-pbody"><p class="sb-note">Read a step, then write why it follows from the step before. Don&#39;t restate it; justify it.</p><p class="sb-c-step"><b>1</b>Revenue rose 20% while the number of customers stayed flat over the same quarter, so average revenue per customer must have risen by roughly that same 20%.</p><h2 class="sb-h">Why does this follow?</h2><div class="sb-lines"><div class="sb-rule"></div><div class="sb-rule"></div></div><p class="sb-c-step"><b>2</b>Most of that rise came from the enterprise tier specifically, which was the one segment of the whole product that got repriced back in March this year.</p><h2 class="sb-h">Why does this follow?</h2><div class="sb-lines"><div class="sb-rule"></div><div class="sb-rule"></div></div><p class="sb-c-step"><b>3</b>Churn in the enterprise tier did not change at all after the repricing took effect, so demand in that tier is evidently not very price-sensitive.</p><h2 class="sb-h">Why does this follow?</h2><div class="sb-lines"><div class="sb-rule"></div><div class="sb-rule"></div></div><p class="sb-c-step"><b>4</b>Therefore a similar, carefully staged repricing of the team tier is worth testing on a small customer segment first before rolling it out further.</p><h2 class="sb-h">Why does this follow?</h2><div class="sb-lines"><div class="sb-rule"></div><div class="sb-rule"></div></div></div><footer class="sb-pfoot"><div class="sb-legend"><span><span class="sb-letter">Q</span> ask</span><span><span class="sb-letter">R</span> stop</span><span><span class="sb-letter">G</span> keep</span><span>X crux = highlighter</span><span><span class="sb-letter">O</span> maybe</span><span><span class="sb-letter">P</span> sense</span><span><span class="sb-letter">D</span> draft</span><span>B reason = black</span><span class="sb-legend-id">W1-P1</span></div></footer></section>
</body>
</html>
